{
  "_note": "What a model must be like to go in the game: read by npm run check-models, npm run import and the part preview page, and written out in plain English in docs/MODELLING_GUIDE.md (npm run guide rewrites its tables from this file). Lengths in metres, in the socket's frame (the car frame for a car): +x the car's left, +y up, +z forward. size: [min, max] of the model's extent along each axis. origin: where the model's origin (its socket) must be on each axis — centre (the middle of the model), min / max (its lowest / highest point: left, down or back is min), within (anywhere inside it) — give or take originTolerance. triangles: the budget (over it: a warning; over twice it: a failure). density: kg per m³ of the model's volume, for the mass the importer estimates (clamped to massRange).",
  "originTolerance": 0.03,
  "textureMaxSize": 1024,
  "materials": {
    "_note": "The material names a model may use: paint is the car's paint (it follows the player's colour), car_atlas the shared colour-palette texture, glass and light_* the car's own (light_aux: an extra lamp: fog lights, light bars, underglow — it glows the part's light colour), rim_finish a rim's face (it takes the rim's finish: chrome, black…), caliper and seat_fabric surfaces in their own colour that keep it whatever the part's finish, and any finish in data/finishes.json (chrome, carbon, titanium, raw_metal…) for surfaces that are always that finish",
    "names": ["paint", "car_atlas", "glass", "rim_finish", "caliper", "seat_fabric"],
    "patterns": ["^light_[a-z0-9_]+$"],
    "finishes": true
  },
  "icon": {
    "_note": "Icons: a transparent PNG size × size, drawn from azimuth (degrees round +y from the front, +90 = the car's left) and elevation; the paint drawn in paintColour so every icon matches",
